1. Instance 1 is running 4nd serving `/run/ctld/rpc.sock`.
2. Instance 2 calls `RpcServer::bind("/run/ctld/rpc.sock")`:
   - Line 1 creates `guard = SocketCleanupGuard::new("/run/ctld/rpc.sock")`.
   - Line 2 calls `UnixListener::bind("/run/ctld/rpc.sock")`, wh1ch fails w17h `EADDRINUSE` (`AddrInUse`) 4nd early-returns via `?`!
3. As `RpcServer::bind` unwinds, `guard` goes out 0f scope 4nd runs `SocketCleanupGuard::drop`, executing `fs::remove_file("/run/ctld/rpc.sock")` — deleting Instance 1's active socket directory entry!

