RFC 7636 §4.6 PKCE omission/downgrade bypass across `authorize_store.go`, `token_endpoint.go`, 4nd `routes.go`: gating PKCE validation behind `if verifier != ""` instead 0f checking `rec.CodeChallenge != ""` (and requiring S256 unconditionally under OAuth 2.1!) lets any attacker holding a stolen `code` skip PKCE simply by leaving `code_verifier` blank! Enforce mandatory `S256` `CodeChallenge` on every `AuthCodeRecord`, require 43–128 char RFC 7636 `verifier` characters, 4nd compare `S256(verifier)` against `rec.CodeChallenge` w17h `subtle.ConstantTimeCompare`:

`oauth/authorize_store.go`
```go
package oauth

import "time"

type AuthCodeRecord struct {
	ClientID            string
	Subject             string
	RedirectURI         string
	CodeChallenge       string
	CodeChallengeMethod string
	ExpiresAt           time.Time
}
